# What a device printed is data, not text.
#
# Git on Windows rewrites the line endings of files it takes for text when it
# checks them out. For source code that is harmless. For a recorded capture it
# changes the bytes a parser is tested against, and a test that cuts a capture
# at "          drop\n" finds no such place in a file that now says
# "          drop\r\n": two tests of the QoS read failed on Windows only,
# for exactly that reason, while passing everywhere else.
#
# These paths are checked out byte for byte as they were committed, on every
# platform. Some captures and some of the bundled TextFSM templates really do
# contain carriage returns, because that is what the device or the upstream
# file holds; this keeps those too.
crates/nocturne-drivers/tests/profiles/** -text
crates/nocturne-textfsm/tests/** -text
crates/nocturne-textfsm/templates/** -text
crates/nocturne-tools/tests/data/** -text
